            "review_title": "Review at Huong Mai",
            "review_text": "Maison Nhã\nHanoi, Vietnam129 contributions\n0\nDelicious Dish\nDec 2024 • Solo\nNgũ Xã is famous for its phở cuốn, and as a visitor, I had to give it a try. The dish is essentially fresh rice noodle sheets rolled with beef and herbs, served with a tangy dipping sauce. It’s light, refreshing, and incredibly satisfying, especially on a warm day.\n\nThe area is bustling, with small eateries lining the streets, each claiming to have the best phở cuốn. I tried a spot recommended by a local, and the rolls were soft, generously filled, and paired perfectly with the sweet and savory dipping sauce.\n\nThe setting is very casual, with low plastic chairs and a lively street vibe. It's not fancy, but it adds to the authentic experience. If you’re visiting Hanoi, stopping by Ngũ Xã for phở cuốn is a must—it’s simple, delicious, and gives you a true taste of local life.\nRead more\nWritten December 28, 2024",
