            "review_text": "MinhNguyen2205\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam18 contributions\n0\nMy worst meal in Hanoi\nJul 2017 • Couples\nRecommended by a friend, I used google map to go there. After many tries, I reached there and surprisingly Huong Mai was a very big restaurant in the area with green staff uniform. I ordered the signature \"Pho cuon\" and one \"Pho tron\". The staff put one portion of \"Pho cuon\" into the microwave placed in front of me. I was shocked! I couldn't imagine the way they prepared my their signature dish. After like 60 seconds, the \"Pho cuon\" was ready on my desk. Let's imagine a disk which is heated in the microwave for 60 seconds, how could it be well heated? It was mid-heated, the beef inside was still cold. The sauce was totally cold as well. The \"Pho tron\" was a bit hotter but the taste was plain. \n\nI was very surprised with the way they re-heat the food and the terrible taste of the dishes. I went out of the restaurant and went around the area. I saw some different family restaurants serving \"Pho cuon\" and all of them served it hot, that was the only expectation of mine! \n\nOne more thing was the hygiene. I asked for a cup of ice to drink mineral water and they gave me a plastic cup with black mark on it and a lot of dust. \n\nIn conclusion, it was my worst meal during my 3 day trip to Hanoi. Never recommend this restaurant to my friend.\nRead more\nWritten July 13, 2017",
